# Deferred push (Mac mini CI/CD)

This repo (`knowledge-base-bot`) deploys on push. The Cursor agent often runs **inside** that same process on the Mac mini. A `git push` to `develop`/`main` can **kill the agent mid-reply**.

## Required workflow

1. Finish **all** code, tests, and the user-facing answer **first**.
2. Only then: `git commit` + `git push` (last actions in the turn).
3. After a backend push, **do not continue** with more tool calls or long follow-up work in the same turn — the session may die. Tell the user the push landed and that a **new chat** may be needed if the agent disconnects.

## Do NOT

- Push “early” to “kick CI” while still implementing features
- Push backend and then keep editing / running long commands in the same turn
- Assume the agent will survive redeploy

## OK without delay

- Local commits without push
- Pushing **other** repos (e.g. `knowledge-base-app-ios`) — that does not redeploy this backend
- Answering the user after push in **one short** final message (no more tools)

## If both iOS and backend changed

1. Push **iOS** first (safe).
2. Finish the reply.
3. Push **backend last**, then stop.
